# Biome never had a Markdown/MDX or YAML printer, so none of these were ever
# reformatted. Prettier does support them, but its printers don't share this
# repo's style: Markdown tables get column-padded and *em* is rewritten to
# _em_ (verified against LINTING.md/DEVELOPMENT.md and the docs/*.mdx pages),
# and YAML is reindented to this config's tabWidth: 4 regardless of the
# file's own 2-space convention (verified against .github/workflows/ci.yml).
# Both would rewrite dozens of files - the changesets backlog, every docs
# page, all four workflow files - that this PR does not otherwise touch, on
# top of the 28 PRs already stacked on this branch. Keep formatting scoped to
# what Biome actually covered: JS/TS/JSX/TSX and JSON. The same is true of
# apps/examples/index.html: Biome has no HTML printer either, and Prettier's
# default 2-space HTML output does not match this repo's tabWidth: 4.
